# Dragged with the mouse half past the screen's edge and let go, Arc's Picture in Picture window
# springs back into the nearest corner, 10 pt in; a two-finger swipe already threw it there. Cra
# left it half off the screen and opened the next video there too (GitHub #332). Here the window is
# let go half past the right edge, then the left, the way a mouse drag ends (no pointer: the test
# copy runs in the background), and must fly fully on screen; the next PiP must open on screen.
# promise: #332
from://open?url=file://${FIXTURES}/Pages/video.html
expect-log loaded file:
wait 2
from://debug?cdp=Runtime.evaluate&params={"expression":"document.getElementById('v').requestPictureInPicture().then(()=>'pip:open')","awaitPromise":true,"userGesture":true}
expect-log Cra cdp Runtime.evaluate .*"value":"pip:open"
wait 1
from://debug?pip=open
expect-log Cra pip open: windows=1 .* onScreen=1
from://debug?pipDrop=right
expect-log pip: dropped past the edge, to (topRight|bottomRight)
wait 2
from://debug?pip=right
expect-log Cra pip right: windows=1 .* onScreen=1
from://debug?pipDrop=left
expect-log pip: dropped past the edge, to (topLeft|bottomLeft)
wait 2
from://debug?pip=left
expect-log Cra pip left: windows=1 .* onScreen=1
from://debug?cdp=Runtime.evaluate&params={"expression":"document.exitPictureInPicture().then(()=>'pip:closed')","awaitPromise":true,"userGesture":true}
expect-log Cra cdp Runtime.evaluate .*"value":"pip:closed"
wait 1
from://debug?cdp=Runtime.evaluate&params={"expression":"document.getElementById('v').requestPictureInPicture().then(()=>'pip:again')","awaitPromise":true,"userGesture":true}
expect-log Cra cdp Runtime.evaluate .*"value":"pip:again"
wait 1
from://debug?pip=again
expect-log Cra pip again: windows=1 .* onScreen=1
